{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Ger.</b> It alone means a temporary resident." "<b>Vetoshav.</b> It is a stranger who dwells in the land. He said: Behold, I am a toshav with you, and death is decreed upon me. And I have no place that would be a holding for me as an inheritance, or a place that I acquire with money, to be a burial ground for the dead."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:28.087437290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}